0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I don't think is right talking about &quot; suspension of disbelief&quot;. I mean... they are gods. In a Neo fantasy/ noir fantasy/ epic metropolitan fantasy like this u can't ask for suspension of disbelief. is like... talking about how bad new york has been destroyed in Godzilla. They are gods. Odin killed a god, this could be a sacrifice he did for himself so NOW and just now he have the power to do a great curse, don't you think? but we're talking to early, we don't really know what will happen', but what we know is: the bullets are cursed.<br /> <br /> talking about odin... he's kinda a jerk. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T05:45:55-07:00","id":1100791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1087902-american-gods?p=1100782#post1100782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I don't think is right talking about &quot; suspension of disbelief&quot;. I mean... they are gods. In a Neo fantasy/ noir fantasy/ epic metropolitan fantasy like this u can't ask for suspension of disbelief. is like... talking about how bad new york has been destroyed in Godzilla. They are gods. Odin killed a god, this could be a sacrifice he did for himself so NOW and just now he have the power to do a great curse, don't you think? but we're talking to early, we don't really know what will happen', but what we know is: the bullets are cursed.<br /> <br /> talking about odin... he's kinda a jerk. </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> suspension of disbelief is defined by the willingness of the audience to believe in the reality the story is telling. It is a must thing to enjoy every story, or else the crowd starts questioning the story they are watching. The writer defines the reality the story takes place in, and as long as the story doesn't contradict the laws of that universe, the crowd is willing to suspend their disbelief and enjoy the story. There is no story without a suspension of disbelief, for once people stop believing in what the story tells, they don't care about it anymore. This is one of the most important things for writing a good story.<br /> <br /> Now, the law of reality defined in American Gods is that their universe is almost like our universe, with only one difference- gods are real. Gods are defined by the things people have faith in, and that they require that faith to exist. As long as people remember their gods, they should exist. Once forgotten, the gods die. As far as I understand (as I haven't read the books), that's the law for American Gods's universe. Now, killing a god is possible- gods do it all the time in mythology, but true death seem to have been defined through being forgotten. While Vulcan has been presented as gaining a great push at his worship through working with the New Gods and having a company at his name, we know who Vulcan is, and that even without the weapon company he should be at least in the same state as Odin in terms of being remembered or honored. We also know that Vulcan is a real place named after that god. As far as I understand the story until now, the events shown in it are not going to end with the change of the world as we know it- it is not some sort of apocalyptic story, or that it is about the future of the world. It is about the present, or maybe the past. The key for American Gods's universe is by being similar enough to our universe. If people would start forget about a god which we, as an audience, still remember, or talk about a collapse of a place which we, as an audience, know is still around, the suspension of disbelief starts to strain- not collapse, just strain. That's a dangerous thing to do. This is not a good story. That's how I get bored- and for stories, there is nothing more dangerous than getting bored of them.<br /> <br /> At least, that's my world view, both as an audience and a writer.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T07:25:05-07:00","id":1100821,"title":"","content":"That may be the end of this exact Vulcan, but it isn't like the idea of Vulcan is dead. Just this particular incarnation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T07:53:35-07:00","id":1100830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1087902-american-gods?p=1100821#post1100821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That may be the end of this exact Vulcan, but it isn't like the idea of Vulcan is dead. Just this particular incarnation</div> </div> </div> </div>Or in Scion terms - dead is this Vulcan Scion, not the Vulcan God that send him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Death of Vulcan does not mean death of town Vulcan, Virigina. Community just will not have blessing of it's god, so it can take <i>decades</i> before having real problem...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-06-2017, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T23:38:57-07:00","id":1101126,"title":"","content":"The answer with regard to the book metaphysics is pretty unambiguous<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Vulcan will eventually show up again, but it won't be the same guy. Just as there are multiple Jesi, and different Odins in other countries, so too will there be a different Vulcan to fill the space emptied by the one who was killed.<br /> <br /> Unless he's ever forgotten, in which case there won't be. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T09:54:31-07:00","id":1101272,"title":"","content":"as I said before, I haven't read the book- so that was me trying to understand how the universe of American Gods work. If it is just as you said, I have no problem with that. Noragami (which I assume was greatly inspired by American Gods to the point I now call it &quot;Japanese Gods&quot;) seem to use the same path, and as long as the metaphysics doesn't contradict itself, all is well. Thanks for the clarification, everyone!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T08:23:41-07:00","id":1101648,"title":"","content":"Vulcan and this entire subplot didn't exist in the original book (At the time Gaiman wrote it there was no evidence that the Greeks or Romans ever made it to America, and he thought that if any mythology was overdone at the time it was the Greco-Roman pantheon), so we're in uncharted territory a bit here. I don't remember Wednesday murdering anyone at this point in the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T12:28:41-07:00","id":1101704,"title":"","content":"I felt Fuller politically overplayed his hand with the clear Nazi imagery. The points about the blood sacrifices for corporate profits and for gun culture were absolutely worth making! But I think going after insularity and racism at the same time diluted the message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T01:44:27-07:00","id":1102734,"title":"","content":"kinda want to make Anpu and Djeheuty a couple now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check o